BUILD
  index.html: hero with email capture, 3 feature plates, static ledger teaser,
  3 operator cards with headshots, 3 rate plates, closing CTA, footer.
  demo.html: TONIGHT'S LEDGER settlement console. 14 rodent lines, species
  filter chips, settled/unsettled segmented control, live search, click or
  Enter on a row opens a receipt modal with a fee breakdown and skeletal
  match readout, and "Run pellet reconciliation" steps the unsettled lines
  one at a time at 260ms and flags exactly one mismatch.
  Both files are self-contained, inline CSS and JS, no frameworks, no CDN
  beyond the Google Fonts import.

WARNINGS / NEAR-MISSES
  - Receipt modal math was initially arbitrary (gross derived from a fudge
    factor). Fixed before validation so the breakdown reconciles against the
    fee shown in the table: gross = (fee - 0.30) / rate.
  - Three of the last seven entries were dark-mode. Not a rule violation, but
    worth flagging for whoever rolls tomorrow: a light direction would give
    the gallery carousel some relief.

VISUAL CHECK (step 9, ran)
  Playwright chromium already present. 2 captures, 2 corrective edits,
  1 re-capture. Well inside the caps.
  Breakage found and fixed: in demo.html the ledger cell buttons use
  `all:unset`, which resets box-sizing to content-box. With width:100% plus
  32px horizontal padding, every cell button overflowed its column, so mass
  ran into property ("31 gHalloway Bros.") and fee ran into state
  ("$0.90Settled") across all 14 rows. Added box-sizing:border-box.
  Second edit: the static ledger teaser on index.html claimed 11 catches and
  412 g while the live demo reports 14 and 502 g. Teaser corrected to match.
  Re-capture confirms columns are clean and nothing else regressed.
  Landing capture: no overlap, no off-canvas elements, hero scrim resolves to
  solid ground under the headline, all four images at correct aspect.

